{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_993f26b5b0c84dc8a8c42f83389fcfbf","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2ed1c888f692d25f45055a745e8c0ce0ec7717c0d97ab68492b861eeb96941f5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"shinpr/galley@b542bd7adb37 snapshot b672269c9deea4f0","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0266283abe39a6c0bdde2b7d13af757d373430ce29a72eac6683d53fc93e2ac7"],"source_ids":["src_b2bd6f48619d5e72b1f8230a0409b15c"],"text":"Task YAML is trusted local input describing goal, acceptance criteria, scope, executor overrides, verification, and worktree, with a documented reference at docs/task-yaml.md.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_993f26b5b0c84dc8a8c42f83389fcfbf"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_993f26b5b0c84dc8a8c42f83389fcfbf","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_34e8458e64599f828f575cd85fd5e73cb00c70ff47a9adf0b4e22b3843ca49bb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"shinpr/galley@b542bd7adb37 snapshot b672269c9deea4f0","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0266283abe39a6c0bdde2b7d13af757d373430ce29a72eac6683d53fc93e2ac7"],"source_ids":["src_b2bd6f48619d5e72b1f8230a0409b15c"],"text":"Executor and supervisor model fields resolve from the task, then the environment profile; only the executor cli has a built-in default (claude), and empty model/effort values defer to the provider CLI's defaults.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_993f26b5b0c84dc8a8c42f83389fcfbf"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_993f26b5b0c84dc8a8c42f83389fcfbf","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6d00c05fdd0b4ad5e18e6abdfa193bdab2835d5186e3b1bc5c0ed0fee6e5dbc7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"shinpr/galley@b542bd7adb37 snapshot b672269c9deea4f0","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7d8c0a1a3432633b2fe2893f16186a5eb9d671251e38d7901e1e166611e7a3f2"],"source_ids":["src_b2bd6f48619d5e72b1f8230a0409b15c"],"text":"The pipeline flows from task YAML plus repository policy through queueing, daemon claim, isolated git worktree execution, supervisor review, then acceptance (PR or local completion), retry within budget, or failure for human review.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_993f26b5b0c84dc8a8c42f83389fcfbf"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_993f26b5b0c84dc8a8c42f83389fcfbf","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7436ed74d467404be417b19607c82aeceb6b27b5da18d045eb28d24ce24c2796","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"shinpr/galley@b542bd7adb37 snapshot b672269c9deea4f0","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c2899abb02ef22302002ee7c3126ba8e02ea19e957751a26168c2bd9f90280e5","slc_d4419c2addb9bab22e05e0962f6489e07e2b61b1e391c41b8f68299dc88a5063"],"source_ids":["src_aed7fe39c4d85fb39e33d52bf96f507d"],"text":"Repository development practice: releases are created from the GitHub UI, triggering a GoReleaser workflow that attaches macOS, Linux, and Windows archives; contributors add CHANGELOG.md entries for user-visible changes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_993f26b5b0c84dc8a8c42f83389fcfbf"}
